 5. 🌴 L.A.&#x27;s socialist civil war 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Los Angeles mayoral candidate Nithya Raman speaks during a campaign event on Saturday. Photo: William Liang/AP A fight over Israel is fracturing the socialist movement just as it stands within reach of capturing the Los Angeles mayor's office, Axios' Russell Contreras writes. 

 Why it matters: The same socialist movement celebrating its ascendancy through New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani is now debating whether to disown Nithya Raman before Los Angeles voters can even weigh in. Leaders of the national Democratic Socialists of America (DSA) face demands to overturn the local chapter's endorsement of Raman over her position on the Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions (BDS) movement against Israel.

 But the L.A. chapter of DSA still enthusiastically endorses Raman, arguing Angelenos deserve a functioning city government. The mayoral race has been defined by homelessness, affordability and public safety. 🧮 By the numbers: Raman leads incumbent Mayor Karen Bass ahead of the Nov. 3 election. A September Berkeley IGS/L.A. Times poll put her ahead 39%-28%, and a more recent Manhattan Institute poll had her up 38%-32%.

